Given heads of two singly linked lists, head1 and head2.  Append the second list to the end of the first list. After performing this operation, return head of the new list .

Examples:

Input: head1: 1 -> 2 -> 3, head2: 4 -> 5
  
Output: 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5

Exaplanation: After joining both lists we get 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5
Constraints:
1 ≤ number of nodes  ≤ 10^5
1 ≤  value of nodes ≤ 10^5

Code:
/* Structure of linked list Node
class Node {
public:
    int data;
    Node* next;

    Node(int x) {
        data = x;
        next = nullptr;
    }
};
*/
class Solution {
  public:
    Node* joinLists(Node* head1, Node* head2) {
        // code here
        Node* temp = head1;
        
        while(temp->next != nullptr){
            temp = temp->next;
        }
        
        temp->next = head2;
        return head1;
    }
};
